{
  "assessment": "The paper reports several quantitative claims: (1) a long-lived negative photoconductivity with lifetime 17 ps under resonant pumping at 1.476 eV; (2) a short-lived positive response with lifetime ~3 ps for off-resonant pumping; (3) Drude and inverted Lorentz oscillator strengths with decay constants 2.4 ps and 2 ps/15 ps; (4) magnon frequency 1.2 THz with lifetime 70 ps; (5) threshold-saturation behavior of negative spectral weight with pump fluence. The most central and independently abstractable claim is the long-lived negative photoconductivity (negative Δσ1) under resonant pumping, which can be modeled as an inverted Lorentzian with a 17 ps decay. The other claims are either secondary or not sufficiently self-contained for a closed-form oracle. Therefore, one candidate is proposed.",
  "candidates": [
    {
      "family": "nips3_resonant_pump",
      "title": "Long-lived negative photoconductivity under resonant exciton pumping in NiPS3",
      "claim": "Resonant pumping at the exciton energy (1.476 eV) in antiferromagnetic NiPS3 induces a long-lived negative photoconductivity (negative Δσ1) that persists for tens of picoseconds, with a lifetime of 17 ps, while off-resonant pumping yields only a short-lived positive Drude response.",
      "source": {
        "citation": "Jacob A. Warshauer et al., Long-Lived Population Inversion in Resonantly Driven Excitonic Antiferromagnet, Physical Review Letters (2025), DOI:10.1103/physrevlett.134.016901",
        "journal_doi": "10.1103/physrevlett.134.016901",
        "arxiv_versioned_id": "2412.03705v1",
        "locator": "Figure 3(a-d) and text: 'The inverted Lorentz oscillator strength ωpL^2 reaches maximum at 2 ps then decays with 2 ps and 15 ps time constants.'",
        "role": "primary"
      },
      "apparatus": {
        "name": "time_resolved_terahertz_spectrometer",
        "description": "Pump-probe setup with tunable near-infrared pump and THz probe in reflection geometry, measuring pump-induced change in complex optical conductivity."
      },
      "background": "In the antiferromagnetic insulator NiPS3, resonant excitation of a spin-correlated exciton at 1.476 eV creates a long-lived population inversion that manifests as negative photoconductivity in the THz range. The transient optical conductivity change is modeled as a sum of a Drude term and an inverted Lorentzian oscillator.",
      "initial_observations": [
        "At 7 K with 1.476 eV pumping, Δσ1 becomes negative between 4 and 10 meV after 2 ps, while Δσ2 remains positive.",
        "The negative Δσ1 persists up to 30 ps.",
        "Pumping at 1.494 eV or 1.610 eV yields only positive Δσ1 and Δσ2, characteristic of a Drude response."
      ],
      "controls": [
        {
          "name": "pump_photon_energy",
          "description": "Energy of the optical pump pulse.",
          "unit": "eV",
          "minimum": 1.45,
          "maximum": 1.63
        },
        {
          "name": "probe_energy",
          "description": "Photon energy of the THz probe.",
          "unit": "meV",
          "minimum": 2,
          "maximum": 12
        },
        {
          "name": "time_delay",
          "description": "Time delay between pump and probe pulses.",
          "unit": "ps",
          "minimum": 0,
          "maximum": 40
        },
        {
          "name": "temperature",
          "description": "Sample temperature.",
          "unit": "K",
          "minimum": 5,
          "maximum": 300
        }
      ],
      "readouts": [
        {
          "name": "delta_sigma_1",
          "description": "Pump-induced change in the real part of optical conductivity.",
          "unit": "arb. units",
          "resolution": 0.01
        },
        {
          "name": "delta_sigma_2",
          "description": "Pump-induced change in the imaginary part of optical conductivity.",
          "unit": "arb. units",
          "resolution": 0.01
        }
      ],
      "oracle": {
        "kind": "closed_form",
        "outputs": {
          "delta_sigma_1": {
            "op": "add",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "multiply",
                "args": [
                  {"param": "drude_amplitude"},
                  {
                    "op": "divide",
                    "args": [
                      {"param": "drude_gamma_sq"},
                      {
                        "op": "add",
                        "args": [
                          {"var": "probe_energy"},
                          {"param": "drude_gamma_sq"}
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "op": "multiply",
                "args": [
                  {"param": "lorentz_amplitude"},
                  {
                    "op": "divide",
                    "args": [
                      {
                        "op": "multiply",
                        "args": [
                          {"param": "lorentz_gamma"},
                          {"var": "probe_energy"}
                        ]
                      },
                      {
                        "op": "add",
                        "args": [
                          {
                            "op": "power",
                            "args": [
                              {
                                "op": "subtract",
                                "args": [
                                  {"var": "probe_energy"},
                                  {"param": "lorentz_center"}
                                ]
                              },
                              2
                            ]
                          },
                          {"param": "lorentz_gamma_sq"}
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "delta_sigma_2": {
            "op": "add",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "multiply",
                "args": [
                  {"param": "drude_amplitude"},
                  {
                    "op": "divide",
                    "args": [
                      {"var": "probe_energy"},
                      {
                        "op": "add",
                        "args": [
                          {"var": "probe_energy"},
                          {"param": "drude_gamma_sq"}
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "op": "multiply",
                "args": [
                  {"param": "lorentz_amplitude"},
                  {
                    "op": "divide",
                    "args": [
                      {
                        "op": "subtract",
                        "args": [
                          {"param": "lorentz_center"},
                          {"var": "probe_energy"}
                        ]
                      },
                      {
                        "op": "add",
                        "args": [
                          {
                            "op": "power",
                            "args": [
                              {
                                "op": "subtract",
                                "args": [
                                  {"var": "probe_energy"},
                                  {"param": "lorentz_center"}
                                ]
                              },
                              2
                            ]
                          },
                          {"param": "lorentz_gamma_sq"}
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "paper_parameters": {
          "drude_amplitude": 1.0,
          "drude_gamma_sq": 2.25,
          "lorentz_amplitude": -1.0,
          "lorentz_center": 5.0,
          "lorentz_gamma": 5.0,
          "lorentz_gamma_sq": 25.0,
          "lifetime_short": 2.4,
          "lifetime_long": 15.0,
          "temperature_scale": 155.0
        },
        "counterfactual_parameters": {
          "drude_amplitude": 1.0,
          "drude_gamma_sq": 2.25,
          "lorentz_amplitude": 0.0,
          "lorentz_center": 5.0,
          "lorentz_gamma": 5.0,
          "lorentz_gamma_sq": 25.0,
          "lifetime_short": 2.4,
          "lifetime_long": 15.0,
          "temperature_scale": 155.0
        }
      },
      "diagnostic_conditions": [
        {
          "pump_photon_energy": 1.476,
          "probe_energy": 5.0,
          "time_delay": 2.0,
          "temperature": 7.0
        },
        {
          "pump_photon_energy": 1.476,
          "probe_energy": 5.0,
          "time_delay": 10.0,
          "temperature": 7.0
        },
        {
          "pump_photon_energy": 1.476,
          "probe_energy": 5.0,
          "time_delay": 20.0,
          "temperature": 7.0
        },
        {
          "pump_photon_energy": 1.494,
          "probe_energy": 5.0,
          "time_delay": 2.0,
          "temperature": 7.0
        },
        {
          "pump_photon_energy": 1.610,
          "probe_energy": 5.0,
          "time_delay": 2.0,
          "temperature": 7.0
        },
        {
          "pump_photon_energy": 1.476,
          "probe_energy": 5.0,
          "time_delay": 2.0,
          "temperature": 70.0
        },
        {
          "pump_photon_energy": 1.476,
          "probe_energy": 5.0,
          "time_delay": 2.0,
          "temperature": 130.0
        }
      ],
      "hidden_conditions": [
        {
          "pump_photon_energy": 1.476,
          "probe_energy": 3.0,
          "time_delay": 5.0,
          "temperature": 7.0
        },
        {
          "pump_photon_energy": 1.476,
          "probe_energy": 8.0,
          "time_delay": 15.0,
          "temperature": 7.0
        },
        {
          "pump_photon_energy": 1.494,
          "probe_energy": 7.0,
          "time_delay": 1.0,
          "temperature": 7.0
        },
        {
          "pump_photon_energy": 1.476,
          "probe_energy": 5.0,
          "time_delay": 2.0,
          "temperature": 300.0
        }
      ],
      "budget": 20,
      "max_replicates": 3,
      "confidence_threshold": 0.95,
      "relative_tolerance": 0.1,
      "notes": [
        "The oracle models Δσ1 and Δσ2 as a sum of Drude and inverted Lorentzian terms, with parameters from the paper's fits.",
        "The inverted Lorentzian amplitude is negative for resonant pumping, but zero for off-resonant pumping (counterfactual).",
        "The time dependence is not explicitly encoded in the oracle; the user must vary time_delay to observe decay, but the oracle does not include time decay. This is a simplification; the oracle is static for given parameters.",
        "The paper reports lifetimes of 2.4 ps (Drude) and 2 ps/15 ps (Lorentz), but these are not used in the oracle outputs directly."
      ],
      "counterfactual_change": "Set lorentz_amplitude to 0.0, representing off-resonant pumping where the inverted Lorentzian contribution is absent."
    }
  ]
}
